{"tool_name":"fastbaps","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"fastbaps","home":"https://github.com/gtonkinhill/fastbaps","license":"MIT","summary":"Fast approximation to a Dirichlet Process Mixture model (DPM) for clustering genetic data.","addition_date":"2019-08-09T13:07:55Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:25Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:fastbaps","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"gqt20@cam.ac.uk","name":"Gerry Tonkin-Hill","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4397-2224","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/gtonkinhill/fastbaps/blob/master/README.md"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Clustering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3432"},{"term":"Essential dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3891"},{"term":"Genotyping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3196"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"fastbaps","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"hans","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/NAR/GKZ361","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 The Author(s) 2019.We present fastbaps, a fast solution to the genetic clustering problem. Fastbaps rapidly identifies an approximate fit to a Dirichlet process mixture model (DPM) for clustering multilocus genotype data. Our efficient model-based clustering approach is able to cluster datasets 10-100 times larger than the existing model-based methods, which we demonstrate by analyzing an alignment of over 110 000 sequences of HIV-1 pol genes. We also provide a method for rapidly partitioning an existing hierarchy in order to maximize the DPM model marginal likelihood, allowing us to split phylogenetic trees into clades and sub-clades using a population genomic model. Extensive tests on simulated data as well as a diverse set of real bacterial and viral datasets show that fastbaps provides comparable or improved solutions to previous model-based methods, while being significantly faster. The method is made freely available under an open source MIT licence as an easy to use R package at https://github.com/gtonkinhill/fastbaps.","authors":[{"name":"Bentley S.D."},{"name":"Corander J."},{"name":"Frost S.D.W."},{"name":"Lees J.A."},{"name":"Tonkin-Hill G."}],"citationCount":32,"date":"2019-06-20T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"Fast hierarchical Bayesian analysis of population structure"},"pmcid":"PMC6582336","pmid":"31076776","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Genotype and phenotype","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0625"},{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0102"},{"term":"Phylogenetics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3293"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"fastbaps","home":"https://bio.tools/fastbaps","license":"MIT","summary":"Fast approximation to a Dirichlet Process Mixture model (DPM) for clustering genetic data.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:fastbaps/lib/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":null,"interpreted":false,"license":null,"public":true,"readme":false,"repository":{"anonymous":null,"online":null}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":222,"citations":[{"count":2,"year":"2019"},{"count":8,"year":"2020"},{"count":22,"year":"2021"},{"count":25,"year":"2022"},{"count":30,"year":"2026"},{"count":35,"year":"2023"},{"count":41,"year":"2024"},{"count":59,"year":"2025"}],"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkz361","pmcid":"PMC6582336","pmid":"31076776","ref_count":34,"refs":[{"count":1,"